2.5 Testing and CI gaps
CI never runs degraded mode. Both matrix legs install swipl, so the supported no-swipl path is only verified by hand.
No backend-parity tests. D3 shipped because nothing compares the two backends.
No performance budgets, no synthetic-ontology generators, no coverage gate, no lint.
Tests are unit-level only. No scenario or golden-transcript corpus.
3. Target architecture (end of cycle)

Key moves:

Reasoner protocol. PythonReasoner and PrologReasoner implement the same contract, and a single semantics spec says what each query kind returns.
Engine / Session facade. It owns sessions, versions, and result schemas. CLI, API, MCP, and the harness are all thin adapters over it.
The harness runs scenarios two ways: in-process, and over MCP. The same scenario file therefore tests the engine and the MCP contract.
