Phase 0: Stabilize
D1/D2: Stop mutating entities. Add OntologyModel.upsert_entity(id, name=None, **attrs), which builds a new frozen Entity and bumps version. Have Entity use a MappingProxyType (or copy on read) so in-place mutation fails loudly.
D4: Track visited import paths (resolved, absolute) and raise ImportCycleError naming the chain. Pull the import logic shared by seam.py and dialog_runner.py into one place.
D5: Key the cache by a model-owned uuid plus version, and bound it with an LRU of about 8 entries.
D7: Escape \n \r \t and control characters in prolog_safe_string.
Docs: Choose one: implement multi-attribute recommend X [k=v, ...] and inline explain (recommended, because the README already promises it and agents will want it), or fix the README. Fix the CLI flag names and the license line. Extend test_docs_verbatim so every README dialog code block gets parsed.
